    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Initial Access / Valid Accounts — Baseline Authentication", "technique": "T1078.002", "what_happened": "At 2026-05-12 09:14:03 CEST, the domain account alice.jones@corp.local successfully authenticated to the corporate OAuth2 token endpoint (10.108.57.10, /oauth2/token, grant_type=password, client_id=corp-mail) from data.srcip=92.184.9.100 — a French IP (OVH, Roubaix, ASN 16276) consistent with the account's normal geolocation baseline. This authentication on its own is unremarkable and establishes the 'normal' reference point for the account.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh logged a successful authentication event for data.win.eventdata.targetUserName=alice.jones with data.srcip / data.win.eventdata.ipAddress=92.184.9.100. No alert fired on this event alone — it is the baseline leg the correlation engine later compares against.", "first_seen": "2026-05-12T09:14:03+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Initial Access / Valid Accounts — Anomalous-Geo Authentication", "technique": "T1078.002", "what_happened": "At 2026-05-12 09:17:41 CEST — only 3 minutes 38 seconds after the French baseline login — the SAME domain account alice.jones@corp.local successfully authenticated again to the same /oauth2/token endpoint, this time from data.srcip=194.165.16.77, a Russian IP (Selectel LLC, Saint-Petersburg, ASN 49505). Three successful authentications were logged from this source between 09:17:41 and 09:18:21. Two successful authentications for the same account from IPs on different continents within under 4 minutes is physically impossible travel — the account is being used concurrently from France and Russia.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh correlation rule 5716 'Same account auth from 2 different geos within 1h' fired: data.win.eventdata.targetUserName=alice.jones with data.srcip=194.165.16.77 (RU) following the same targetUserName from data.srcip=92.184.9.100 (FR) inside the same hour. MITRE T1078.002 (Valid Accounts: Domain Accounts) attached by the rule.", "first_seen": "2026-05-12T09:17:41+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Post-Compromise Impact — Privileged Endpoint Access", "technique": "T1078.002", "what_happened": "Between 09:22:10 and 09:25:55 CEST, the anomalous Russian session (data.srcip=194.165.16.77) used the alice.jones token to access admin-scope API endpoints on 10.108.57.10: /api/admin/users, /api/admin/export and /api/admin/audit-log. alice.jones is a standard mailbox user with no administrative role — admin-scope access from her token, from the anomalous-geo session, is clear post-compromise privileged abuse and a strong account-takeover impact indicator.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 31500 'Admin access from anomalous geo' fired: HTTP access to /api/admin/* paths on data.dstip=10.108.57.10 correlated to the same data.srcip=194.165.16.77 and the same account from rule 5716. The rule chains the impossible-travel authentication to subsequent privileged-resource access.", "first_seen": "2026-05-12T09:22:10+0200"}
